-- APOLLO (LIMS3) target schema: OPTIONAL database protections. Apply after schema.sql.
-- None of this is a function or a trigger. It is three kinds of declarative protection.
--   1. Simple value checks: a CHECK that names one column and calls no function (not blank, not negative, one of a list).
--   2. "Only one in this state" uniqueness: partial unique indexes, which the backend cannot guarantee under concurrent writes.
--   3. Privileges for the application account (lims_app): no DELETE or TRUNCATE anywhere, and append-only
--      (SELECT and INSERT only) on the audit trail, signatures, sign-in events, stored files and stock movements.
-- Recommended for any system that will hold real GxP records (21 CFR Part 11). Remove any section you decide against.
SET search_path = lims, public;

